---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import '../../styles/doc.css';
---
<Base title="Bitcoin Self-Custody: Not Your Keys, Not Your Coins - OpenBitcoin" description="What bitcoin self-custody means: why an exchange balance is a claim on a company, why your seed words are the wallet, and the habits that keep coins safe.">
<main class="wrap doc-wrap">
  <div class="doc-head">
    <div class="doc-kicker">Learn</div>
    <h1>Self-custody</h1>
    <p class="doc-lede">Not your keys, not your coins. What it actually means to hold bitcoin yourself, why the seed words are the wallet, and the small set of habits that make self-custody safe.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="doc-grid">
  <div>
    <div class="sc-card">
      <div class="sc-tlab">What self-custody means</div>
      <p class="sc-p">Bitcoin is controlled by cryptographic keys. Whoever holds the keys to an address can spend the coins on it; nobody else can. Self-custody means those keys are yours: generated by your wallet, known only to you. Custodial holding means a company holds the keys and your account shows a number.</p>
      <div class="sc-compare">
        <div class="sc-col">
          <div class="sc-clab sc-clab-cust">Balance on an exchange</div>
          <ul class="sc-clist">
            <li>The exchange holds the keys; your balance is a row in their database.</li>
            <li>What you own is a claim on the company, like a bank balance without the deposit insurance.</li>
            <li>Withdrawals can be paused, accounts frozen, terms changed.</li>
            <li>If the company fails, you stand in line with its other creditors.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="sc-col">
          <div class="sc-clab sc-clab-self">Coins in your own wallet</div>
          <ul class="sc-clist">
            <li>You hold the keys; the coins are recorded on the chain under them.</li>
            <li>Yours regardless of any company's fate. There is no company in the loop.</li>
            <li>Nothing to freeze, no permission to ask, no counterparty.</li>
            <li>The trade: nobody can reset your password. The responsibility is also yours.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="sc-p sc-pm">Custody has a place: an exchange is where most people buy. The point of this page is what happens after the purchase. A balance left on an exchange is an IOU; coins withdrawn to a wallet whose keys only you hold are bitcoin.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="sc-card sc-mt">
      <div class="sc-tlab">The seed phrase is the wallet</div>
      <p class="sc-p">When a wallet is created it shows you 12 or 24 ordinary English words. Those words encode the master key. Every address the wallet will ever use is derived from them, which means the words <b class="sc-em">are</b> the wallet. The app on your phone and the device in your drawer are just windows onto what the words control.</p>
      <div class="sc-seed" aria-label="A masked 12-word seed phrase, words hidden">
        <div class="sc-word"><i>1</i><b>&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;</b></div>
        <div class="sc-word"><i>2</i><b>&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;</b></div>
        <div class="sc-word"><i>3</i><b>&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;</b></div>
        <div class="sc-word"><i>4</i><b>&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;</b></div>
        <div class="sc-word"><i>5</i><b>&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;</b></div>
        <div class="sc-word"><i>6</i><b>&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;</b></div>
        <div class="sc-word"><i>7</i><b>&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;</b></div>
        <div class="sc-word"><i>8</i><b>&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;</b></div>
        <div class="sc-word"><i>9</i><b>&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;</b></div>
        <div class="sc-word"><i>10</i><b>&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;</b></div>
        <div class="sc-word"><i>11</i><b>&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;</b></div>
        <div class="sc-word"><i>12</i><b>&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;</b></div>
      </div>
      <p class="sc-fine">Masked on purpose. Real seed words never belong on a screen, a photo, or a web page, including this one.</p>
      <div class="sc-verdict"><b>The one rule</b><span>Anyone who has the words has the coins, from anywhere on earth, instantly. And no legitimate person or software will ever ask for them: not support staff, not a wallet update, not a "verification" or "sync" screen, not this site. A request for your seed words is not a step in a process. It is the theft itself.</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="sc-card sc-mt">
      <div class="sc-tlab">How to hold: categories, not brands</div>
      <p class="sc-p">The right setup depends on the amount at stake. These are categories; within each, prefer open-source software and buy any hardware directly from its manufacturer.</p>
      <div class="sc-tiers">
        <div class="sc-tier">
          <div class="sc-tname">Hot wallet</div>
          <div class="sc-tuse">spending money, small amounts</div>
          <p class="sc-tp">An app on your phone or computer. The keys live on an internet-connected device, so treat it like the cash in your pocket: convenient, and capped at what you could stand to lose to malware or a stolen phone.</p>
          <div class="sc-tex">Open-source examples: Electrum, Bitcoin Core</div>
        </div>
        <div class="sc-tier">
          <div class="sc-tname">Hardware signer</div>
          <div class="sc-tuse">savings</div>
          <p class="sc-tp">A dedicated device that generates the keys offline and never reveals them; it signs transactions while the keys stay off your computer entirely. Paired with desktop software that watches the chain and builds the transactions.</p>
          <div class="sc-tex">Open-source companions: Sparrow, Electrum</div>
        </div>
        <div class="sc-tier">
          <div class="sc-tname">Multisig</div>
          <div class="sc-tuse">large holdings</div>
          <p class="sc-tp">Spending requires several keys, commonly 2 of 3, held on separate devices in separate places. One lost or stolen key is no longer fatal. More setup and more discipline, which is the price of removing single points of failure.</p>
          <div class="sc-tex">Coordinated with: Sparrow, Electrum</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sc-card sc-mt">
      <div class="sc-tlab">Backup habits</div>
      <ul class="sc-steps">
        <li><b>Write the words by hand,</b> on paper or stamped into steel. Steel survives the house fire and the burst pipe that paper does not.</li>
        <li><b>Keep them offline, always.</b> No photos, no cloud notes, no password manager, no email draft. The words never touch a keyboard except when you are deliberately restoring a wallet on a device you trust, and never a website under any circumstances.</li>
        <li><b>Test the backup before it matters.</b> Restore the wallet from the written words on a fresh device or a wiped one, and confirm the same addresses appear. An untested backup is a hope, not a backup.</li>
        <li><b>Plan for fire, flood, and heirs.</b> Keep a second copy in a second location, and make sure someone you trust knows the backup exists and how to use it. Coins whose words die with you are gone; the network cannot return them.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="sc-card sc-mt">
      <div class="sc-tlab">Common mistakes</div>
      <ul class="sc-mist">
        <li><b>Screenshotting the seed.</b> Photos sync to the cloud, and the cloud is someone else's computer.</li>
        <li><b>Keeping the words in a notes app.</b> Same problem with extra steps. Malware searches for exactly this.</li>
        <li><b>Typing the words into a website.</b> There is no website that needs them. This is the entire scam; see <a href="/learn/scams">how bitcoin scams work</a>.</li>
        <li><b>Buying a hardware signer secondhand or "pre-configured" from a marketplace.</b> A device that arrives with the words already printed in the box is a trap: the seller kept a copy. Buy new, from the manufacturer, and generate the seed yourself.</li>
        <li><b>Sending the whole balance in the first transaction.</b> Send a small test first, confirm it arrived at your new wallet, then move the rest. The fee for the extra transaction is the cheapest insurance in bitcoin.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="sc-about doc-prose">
      <p>Self-custody is a trade: you remove every counterparty and accept every responsibility. The habits above are most of that responsibility, and none of them are difficult; they are just unforgiving of shortcuts. Before sending to a new address, check it character by character or run it through the <a href="/tools/validate">address validator</a>, and copy it from the source rather than from your history; the <a href="/learn/address-poisoning">address poisoning</a> page explains why. This page is informational, not advice on what to buy or how much to hold; see the <a href="/terms">terms</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <aside class="doc-rail">
    <div class="doc-tile">
      <div class="doc-tlab">In one sentence</div>
      <p class="sc-railp">An exchange balance is a claim on a company; coins secured by seed words only you hold are yours regardless of what happens to any company, which is the entire meaning of "not your keys, not your coins."</p>
    </div>
    <div class="doc-tile">
      <div class="doc-tlab">Related</div>
      <nav>
        <a href="/learn/scams">Bitcoin scams and how they work</a>
        <a href="/learn/address-poisoning">Address poisoning</a>
        <a href="/tools/validate">Address validator and typo locator</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </aside>
  </div>
</main>
<style is:global>
  .sc-card{background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:22px 24px}
  .sc-mt{margin-top:14px}
  .sc-tlab{font:700 9.5px var(--mono);letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-3);margin-bottom:12px}
  .sc-p{font:500 14px/1.65 var(--sans);color:var(--ink-2);margin:0}
  .sc-pm{margin-top:12px}
  .sc-em{color:var(--ink);font-weight:700}
  .sc-compare{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px;margin-top:14px}
  .sc-col{background:var(--field);border:1px solid var(--line-2);border-radius:10px;padding:14px 16px}
  .sc-clab{font:700 9.5px var(--mono);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:7px}
  .sc-clab::before{content:"";width:9px;height:9px;border-radius:2px}
  .sc-clab-cust{color:var(--down)}
  .sc-clab-cust::before{background:var(--down)}
  .sc-clab-self{color:var(--up)}
  .sc-clab-self::before{background:var(--up)}
  .sc-clist{margin:0;padding-left:18px}
  .sc-clist li{font:500 13px/1.6 var(--sans);color:var(--ink-2);margin-top:6px}
  .sc-clist li::marker{color:var(--ink-3)}
  .sc-seed{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:8px;margin-top:14px}
  .sc-word{background:var(--field);border:1px solid var(--line-2);border-radius:8px;padding:8px 10px;display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:8px}
  .sc-word i{font:700 9.5px var(--mono);color:var(--ink-3);font-style:normal;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;min-width:14px;text-align:right}
  .sc-word b{font:700 12px var(--mono);color:var(--ink-2);letter-spacing:2px}
  .sc-fine{font:600 10.5px/1.5 var(--mono);letter-spacing:.04em;color:var(--ink-3);margin:8px 0 0}
  .sc-verdict{margin-top:14px;border-radius:12px;padding:16px 18px;border:1px solid rgba(246,70,93,.45);background:rgba(246,70,93,.07)}
  .sc-verdict b{display:block;font:700 13px var(--mono);letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--down)}
  .sc-verdict > span{display:block;font:500 13.5px/1.6 var(--sans);color:var(--ink-2);margin-top:6px}
  .sc-tiers{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:12px;margin-top:14px}
  .sc-tier{background:var(--field);border:1px dashed rgba(255,166,60,.32);border-radius:10px;padding:14px 16px;min-width:0}
  .sc-tname{font:700 12.5px var(--mono);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink)}
  .sc-tuse{font:700 9px var(--mono);letter-spacing:.11em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--acc);margin-top:3px}
  .sc-tp{font:500 12.5px/1.6 var(--sans);color:var(--ink-2);margin:10px 0 0}
  .sc-tex{font:600 10px/1.5 var(--mono);letter-spacing:.04em;color:var(--ink-3);margin-top:10px;padding-top:8px;border-top:1px dotted var(--line-2)}
  .sc-steps{margin:0;padding-left:22px}
  .sc-steps li{font:500 14px/1.65 var(--sans);color:var(--ink-2);margin-top:9px}
  .sc-steps li::marker{color:var(--acc);font-weight:700}
  .sc-steps b{color:var(--ink);font-weight:600}
  .sc-mist{margin:0;padding-left:0;list-style:none}
  .sc-mist li{font:500 14px/1.65 var(--sans);color:var(--ink-2);margin-top:9px;padding-left:22px;position:relative}
  .sc-mist li::before{content:"\00d7";position:absolute;left:0;top:0;font:700 15px/1.55 var(--mono);color:var(--down)}
  .sc-mist b{color:var(--ink);font-weight:600}
  .sc-mist a{color:var(--acc);text-decoration:none;border-bottom:1px dashed rgba(247,147,26,.35);padding-bottom:1px}
  .sc-mist a:hover{border-bottom-style:solid}
  .sc-about{margin-top:14px}
  .sc-about p{font:500 13.5px/1.65 var(--sans);color:var(--ink-3)}
  .sc-railp{font:500 12px/1.6 var(--sans);color:var(--ink-3);margin:0}
  @media(max-width:900px){.sc-tiers{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
  @media(max-width:700px){.sc-compare{grid-template-columns:1fr}.sc-seed{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr)}}
  @media(max-width:420px){.sc-seed{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}}
</style>
</Base>
